* ''The unwired code takes a zero-trust review first'' (operator, 2026-11-06: //"The unwired code should get zero trust critical reviews before wiring (might be legit old design, might be pono but last steps unfinished design)."//). Code that production never calls (the unwired-code scout at `ffe05bc79`) earns no wiring by its presence: a zero-trust critical review decides retire, wire or reshape, then the work. Its items land before the rite: `L28`, `K22`, `K23` and `P27`.

